{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787029932052252001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"dermatoid-brassy-junco","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"97b1a3f7ed2fcd6a4f5cbd286f4fc209424bc2dbff0931a843f1f639057f9a69","event_uuid":"6cc63685-5fce-4f91-9ae6-da8150eef994","position":{"commit_sha":"11d556885e3b38b42ddb67a9ad64a44ab899d439","position":"1787027525763725001-6cc63685-5fce-4f91-9ae6-da8150eef994"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c09461f04980cd97159edefbe8c57d81bb4821b0f0a04908757250edd5a64641","event_uuid":"05630de6-9313-4999-b30b-b34a69dcb2ab","position":{"commit_sha":"337fac9ab5da9df48d7e4983d0fc15a087cb5246","position":"1787027541270212001-05630de6-9313-4999-b30b-b34a69dcb2ab"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d4362c3102070608354b331f7be422e19a4604e6505ce7d1a91bd7a3019ed5b2","event_uuid":"60bec7e7-80db-4d43-be64-8c92c8f64c22","position":{"commit_sha":"cd7dbd4712ac53b652124754e2681177d1f5b43e","position":"1787027546502609001-60bec7e7-80db-4d43-be64-8c92c8f64c22"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787027525763725001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nAfter repository extraction, `BindingStore` still owns forward/reverse identity transitions, pending/confirmed state, stale reverse cleanup, and immutable numeric-ID moves. These coupled rules need one policy owner and both-index tests.\n\n## Outcome\nCreate the first `BindingLifecycle` slice for bind, confirm, unbind, reverse cleanup, and numeric-ID re-key while the public facade retains all signatures and owns coordination.\n\n## Plan\n1. Start with table-driven failing tests over valid, missing, corrupt, duplicate, and stale forward/reverse combinations.\n2. Move the cohesive identity transition call graph into `binding_lifecycle.py`, operating on repository-owned original dictionaries.\n3. Preserve safety-abort on ambiguous double bind, stale reverse removal, pending/confirmed semantics, immutable numeric-ID re-key, and legacy no-ID behavior.\n4. Delegate existing facade methods without exposing the lifecycle owner or repository to adapters.\n\n## Testing\nReload through the real repository after every transition and assert both indexes plus exact caller-visible outcomes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every valid bind/confirm/unbind transition leaves at most one forward and one matching reverse identity.\n- [ ] Ambiguous double binds safety-abort without guessed deletion.\n- [ ] Stale reverse entries are removed only in the existing permitted cases.\n- [ ] Immutable numeric-ID matches re-key moved issues instead of retiring them.\n- [ ] Legacy records without numeric IDs retain current behavior and facade signatures.\n\n## Out of scope\nAbsence/tombstone/comment policy and rich-emission mutation move to later S2 tasks.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_lifecycle.py","reason":"New cohesive identity-transition policy owner."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Delegate identity operations behind the authoritative facade."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py","reason":"Both-index transition and corruption tables."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_unbind.py","reason":"Stale reverse cleanup regression coverage."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py","reason":"Immutable-ID move and legacy signature oracles."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"fc1c-1b08-70c2-4afb","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp02","binding-lifecycle","tdd"],"ticket_id":"6083-b802-e90a-416e","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S2 T1 — Extract binding identity transitions","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_lifecycle.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_store_unbind.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_binding_move_rekey_heldout.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC5","dd_text":"Identity transitions, ambiguity, reverse cleanup, immutable-ID moves, and legacy compatibility"}]},"source_event_uuids":["6cc63685-5fce-4f91-9ae6-da8150eef994","05630de6-9313-4999-b30b-b34a69dcb2ab","60bec7e7-80db-4d43-be64-8c92c8f64c22"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787029932052252001,"uuid":"920d4c8b-74a9-4bdb-8dca-6402a76bdd8c"}